cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "WeaveMark: A Specification Language for Readable, Reusable, and Composable Prompts"
message: "If WeaveMark helps your research, writing, or software work, please cite it as software."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Salem
    given-names: Paulo
    email: paulosalem@paulosalem.com
    website: "https://www.paulosalem.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/paulosalem/weavemark"
url: "https://paulosalem.github.io/weavemark/"
abstract: >-
  WeaveMark is a Markdown-native specification language for prompts. Authors
  write readable documents woven with directives for reuse, control flow,
  output contracts, and validation; the WeaveMark Processor compiles them into
  concrete prompt artifacts and can execute them through predefined engines.
keywords:
  - llm
  - prompt-engineering
  - prompt-composition
  - specification-language
  - markdown
license: MIT
version: 0.9.4
date-released: "2026-08-03"
